<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="b6fa0356">A roadmap is a structured plan with multiple layers and milestones that defines the path forward on an initiative, project,
or program for moving the organization’s activities from a current state to an agreed-upon future state.</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="d8b367a8"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="cabd3552">&lt;p&gt;
    For short term assessment projects, it may not be possible to obtain detailed information on each initiative, in such
    cases a lighter weight version of the roadmap may be sufficient. For medium to long term assessment projects where
    the client could consider EY for future state implementation, a more detailed version of the roadmap should be
    produced.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="35b6ff0d"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="a2024cb0">To provide a strategic view of the next steps in the project to achieve the desired future state based on the results of
the current state assessment.</attribute>
<attribute name="impactOfNotHaving" nodeId="b087ec11"></attribute>
<attribute name="reasonsForNotNeeding" nodeId="d97b3798"></attribute>
<attribute name="briefOutline" nodeId="6e0ad344">&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        The roadmap should at least contain a brief summary of each of the initiatives identified and a
        high-level timeline that outlines key activities to be performed to get to future state.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        A more comprehensive version of the roadmap will provide more specifics on each of the initiatives such as resource
        plan, roles/responsibilities, organization structure, future state design documents and timeline.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
